{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "description": "Pinned inputs for the project-published media runtime packs (track dub_asr_diar_hardening_20261029, FR-2.6): a static macOS whisper-cli built from source, and mirrored upstream ffmpeg builds. Consumed by scripts/lock_media_runtime.py (plan/fetch/stage/smoke/pack/lock) and scripts/render_media_runtime_manifests.py, driven by .github/workflows/media-runtime-build.yml. Nothing here enters pyproject.toml or the frozen bundle; only the rendered src/vienetts_app/core/media_runtime_manifests.json ships.",
 "downloadsBase": "https://nguyensitrung.github.io/VieNeuTTSApp/packs",
 "packDir": "media",
 "maxPackBytes": 100000000,
 "notes": [
  "Packs are published on gh-pages, a git branch: GitHub rejects any pushed file over 100 MiB, so the lock refuses a pack over 100 MB (decimal).",
  "Published pack names carry the first 12 hex digits of their SHA-256, so a rebuild never replaces bytes an already-shipped manifest pins.",
  "Pack layout (core/ai_models.py installers): bin/<executables> at the archive root, plus LICENSE and SOURCE.txt; Linux ffmpeg packs add lib/ (RUNPATH $ORIGIN/../lib).",
  "ffmpeg picks: BtbN FFmpeg-Builds gpl-shared for Windows/Linux (the gpl static archives are 120-185 MiB, over the gh-pages limit; shared libs are the libav* family only, every other dependency is static) and ffmpeg.martin-riedl.de release builds for macOS. martin-riedl.de Linux builds are configured with --enable-nonfree and are NOT redistributable, so they are not used.",
  "Upstream pins were read on 2026-10-29 from the published checksum files as data (BtbN checksums.sha256, martin-riedl.de per-file .sha256), with sizes from the GitHub release API and HTTP Content-Length. The BtbN month-end build is kept for two years (BtbN README); the daily builds are pruned after 14 days.",
  "An unfilled pin (size <= 0, or a sha256 / commit that is not hex) is a placeholder: plan, fetch, lock and render all refuse that cell until it is filled from the upstream checksum file."
 ],
 "runtimes": {
  "whisper_cpp": {
